// Both operands are undefined, so which name the diagnostic reports says which one
// was elaborated first. The reference builds this pair as a tuple, and OCaml
// evaluates a tuple's components right to left - so it names the RIGHT one.
//
// The port used to name the left. That is not a cosmetic difference: it is the
// evaluation order of a mirrored arm, visible in the emission as instantiation
// order and here as the first line a user reads.
fn main() { println(nope_a + nope_b); }
